   - Length variance (difference between outputs and references).
 - Report generation: structured JSON + Markdown summaries.
 - CLI command `frai eval` wrapping the core harness.
+- Threshold validation: gate CI/CD on metrics via `--threshold <metric>=<min>` (exit code 1 on failure, 2 on invalid input).
 
 ## Data Expectations
 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Threshold Validation (CI Gating)
+- `generateReport` accepts an optional `thresholds` object mapping metric IDs to minimum scores (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }`).
+- CLI: `frai eval --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95` (can be given multiple times).
+- Threshold logic:
+  - Passes if `metric.score >= threshold`.
+  - Fails if `metric.score === null` (metric has no valid score).
+  - Reports include `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array with per-metric pass/fail details.
+- Exit codes:
+  - 0 if all thresholds pass (or no thresholds given).
+  - 1 if any threshold fails.
+  - 2 if threshold format is invalid (not `<metric>=<number>`) or metric/value is unknown.
+- Markdown reports gain a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL per metric.
+- JSON reports gain top-level `passed` and `thresholds` fields.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
+- SDK users can pass custom metric IDs in the `thresholds` object to `generateReport` if they register custom metrics with `runEvaluations`.
 
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
